\newpage
\begin{verbatim}
%
% TRANSFORMATION Tfincontrol1  (* cree que nada *) 
< m1:CLAUSE{CLAUSErec1}
           [ mu1,
             I1:subjrel/T1,
             mu2,
             predrel/VERBP{VERBPrec1}[mu7,head/VERB{VERBrec1}[mu8],mu9],
             mu10,
             complrel/I3::SENTENCE{SENTENCErec1}
                [ I4:mu4, I2:subjrel/T2, I5:mu5 ],
             mu6
           ]
>

< m :CLAUSE{CLAUSErec1}
           [ mu1,
             I1:subjrel/T1,
             mu2,
             predrel/VERBP{VERBPrec1}[mu7,head/VERB{VERBrec1}[mu8],mu9],
             mu10,
             complrel/I3::SENTENCE{SENTENCErec1}
                [ I4:mu4, 
                  I5:mu5 
                ],
             mu6
           ]
>



   MATCHCONDITIONS
      <
       I1: T1.CAT IN [NPVAR, CNVAR]
       I2: T2.CAT IN [NPVAR, CNVAR]
       I3: SENTENCErec1.finiteness = finite AND 
           SENTENCErec1.mood = declarative
       I4: ALL(mu4, I41:rel1/..)
           I41: rel1 IN [leftdislocrel, shiftrel, conjrel]
       I5: ALL(mu5, I51:rel2/..) 
           I51: rel2 <> subjrel AND QUOTE_Srelprec(subjrel, rel2)
      >

<
   SUBRULE
      < T1:NPVAR{NPVARrec1}
        T2:NPVAR{NPVARrec2}
      >
      < T1:NPVAR{NPVARrec1}
      >

      COMP
         <
          C1: NPVARrec1 = NPVARrec2 EXCEPT FOR [cases] AND
              NPVARrec2.cases = [Nominative] AND
              VERBrec1.controller = subject
          A1: @ 
         >

   SUBRULE
      < T1:CNVAR{CNVARrec1}
        T2:CNVAR{CNVARrec2}
      >
      < T1:CNVAR{CNVARrec1}
      >

      COMP
         <
          C1: CNVARrec1 = CNVARrec2 EXCEPT FOR [cases] AND
              CNVARrec2.cases = [Nominative] AND
              VERBrec1.controller = subject
          A1: @ 
         >
  
>

&

\end{verbatim}

\newpage
\begin{description}
\item[* name:] Tfincontrol1
\item[* relevant examples:]
x1 cree [que x1 esta enfermo ]  --> x1 cree que \'{e}l esta enfermo\\
\item[* language:] (Dutch) 
\item[* kind of rule:]  M-rule
\item[* subgrammar:]  XPProptoCLAUSE
\item[* class:] (name of rule, transformation or filter class) TC_NOC
\item[* date of creation:]   17-JAN-1989 14:10:47 
\item[* author:] Jan Odijk
\item[* copied from:] dutch finite control
\item[* modification:]\mbox{}
\begin{enumerate}
\item date: ../../..\ \ \ \ \ author:
\item date: ../../..\ \ \ \ \ author:
\end{enumerate}
\item[* task:] to take care of subject control into finite complements.
(in generation only). It is intended to be used when a translation occurred from
an infinite open sentence into a finite sentence.
\item[\ \ strategy:] (also: deviations from accepted proposals)
The subject variable is spelled out as a personaal pronoun.
1p sg, m -> yo (m)( creo que (yo) estoy enfermo)\\
1p sg, f -> yo (f)( creo que (yo) estoy enferma)\\
2p sg, m -> t\'{u} (m)( crees que (t\'{u}) est\'{a}s enfermo)\\
2p sg, f -> t\'{u} (f)( crees que (t\'{u}) est\'{a}s enferma)\\
3p sg, m -> \'{el}( el hombre cree que (\'{e}l) est\'{a} enfermo)\\
3p sg, f -> ella ( la mujer cree que (ella) est\'{a} enferma)\\
1p pl, m -> nosotros (nosotros creemos que (nosotros) estamos enfermos)\\
1p pl, f -> nosotras (nosotras creemos que (nosotras) estamos enfermas)\\
2p pl, m -> vosotros (vosotros creiste que (vosotros) est\'{a}is enfermos)\\
2p pl, f -> vosotras (vosotras creiste que (vosotras) est\'{a}is enfermas)\\
3p pl, m -> ellos (ellos creen que (ellos) est\'{a}n enfermos)\\
3p pl, f -> ellas (ellas creen que (ellas) est\'{a}n enfermas)\\

!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!
The treatment of usted, ustedes is yet completely wrong, though without bad 
effects in the output. When usted, ustedes is the antecedent, the variable is
spelled out as one of the pronouns \'{e}l, ella, ellos or ellas. A correct 
treatment would require the attribute cortesia on NP and NPVAR.
!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!

\item[\ \ rejected alternatives:]
\item[\ \ clarification of variables:]
\item[\ \ clarification of the splitting up into subrules:]
\item[\ \ clarification of the collapsing of rules:] (e.g. clarification of parameters)
